IMPORT prelude

-- Traditional Chinese Medicine Practitioners Act 2000 (Singapore) -- what the Act decides for a practitioner, an employer, a patient
-- and a complainant: what counts as the practice of traditional Chinese medicine (s 2), who may practise and the offences of
-- unlawful practice and unlawful employment (ss 24, 25), the duties to notify changes, renew and surrender certificates (ss 12, 16,
-- 17), the Board's disciplinary powers and when its decisions take effect (ss 19, 21, 23), voluntary cancellation (s 26A),
-- complaints (ss 26B, 26C), the duty to answer an investigator (ss 29(8), 30(5), (6)) and composition (s 34A).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition ("incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"), informal consolidation
-- (version in force from 5/12/2025), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/TCMPA2000.txt. The latest amendment annotated is
-- Act 19 of 2025 (Statutes (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2025, in force 5 December 2025), annotated at s 34 (service of
-- documents). THE SCHEDULE (substances whose preparation or supply is a practice of TCM under s 2(e)) is EMPTY in the .txt deposit:
-- only its heading survived extraction.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0022 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. SCOPED to the provisions a practitioner, a clinic or a patient meets. Not encoded: the Board, its membership and
-- committees (ss 3-11, 27, 32), the contents of the Register (ss 12(1), 13, 18), the regulation-making powers (ss 14(4), 36), the
-- course of an inquiry and its timetable (ss 26E-26G, 26I-26K), interim-order procedure beyond its effect on the practising
-- certificate (s 26H), investigators' entry, search and seizure (ss 28, 29(1)-(7), 30A), funds, costs, service and exemptions
-- (ss 20, 31, 33-35). WHICH practices are "prescribed" is decided by Ministerial order under s 14(1) and is not in the deposit, so
-- it is an input here.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Traditional Chinese Medicine Practitioners Act 2000 -- practice`

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` x y MEANS IF x AT MOST y THEN x ELSE y

§§ `2 -- the practice of traditional Chinese medicine`

-- s 2: "practice of traditional Chinese medicine" means (a) acupuncture (including "cupping and moxibustion"); (b) "the diagnosis,
-- treatment, prevention or alleviation of any disease ... or the prescription of any herbal medicine"; (c) "the regulation of the
-- functional states of the human body"; (d) preparing or supplying herbal medicine on a prescription; (e) preparing or supplying
-- a Schedule substance; (f) "the processing of any herbal medicine"; (g) "the retailing of any herbal medicine", -- all "on the
-- basis of traditional Chinese medicine". "retailing" means selling to a person "who obtains the herbal medicine other than for the
-- purpose of wholesale". Selling herbs wholesale is therefore not retailing (an inference from the definition: wholesale selling,
-- without processing, is in no paragraph).
DECLARE Activity IS ONE OF
    `acupuncture`
    `cupping or moxibustion`
    `diagnosing or treating a disease`
    `prescribing herbal medicine`
    `regulating the functional states of the body`
    `supplying herbal medicine on a prescription`
    `processing herbal medicine`
    `retailing herbal medicine`
    `selling herbal medicine wholesale`

GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity, `on the basis of traditional Chinese medicine` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the activity is a practice of traditional Chinese medicine` IF
        `on the basis of traditional Chinese medicine`
    AND CONSIDER `the activity`
        WHEN `selling herbal medicine wholesale` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `24, 25 -- who may practise, and the offences`

-- s 24(6): a "qualified person" is one who is "(a) registered to carry out; and (b) has in force a practising certificate which
-- authorises the person to carry out" the prescribed practice. s 19(9): while a registration "remains suspended, he or she is not
-- to be regarded as a registered person".
GIVEN `registered` IS A BOOLEAN, `suspended` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds a practising certificate in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a qualified person` IF
    `registered` AND (NOT `suspended`) AND `holds a practising certificate in force`

-- s 24(1): a person must not (a) carry out any prescribed practice or (b) "advertise or otherwise hold himself or herself out to be
-- qualified" to carry it out, "unless he or she is a qualified person ... and he or she carries out that prescribed practice in
-- accordance with the conditions of his or her registration". Subject to transitional regulations (s 24(3)), not modelled.
GIVEN `the practice is prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN, `practises or holds out` IS A BOOLEAN, `registered` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `suspended` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds a practising certificate in force` IS A BOOLEAN, `within the registration conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `practising is an offence under section 24(1)` IF
        `the practice is prescribed`
    AND `practises or holds out`
    AND NOT (    `the person is a qualified person` `registered` `suspended` `holds a practising certificate in force`
             AND `within the registration conditions`)

-- s 24(2): a person must not employ a person "who is not a qualified person" to carry out the prescribed practice. (5): "it is a
-- defence for the accused to prove that (a) the accused did not know ... and (b) the accused had exercised due diligence".
GIVEN `the practice is prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN, `employs someone to carry it out` IS A BOOLEAN, `the employee is qualified` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `did not know` IS A BOOLEAN, `exercised due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `employing is an offence under section 24(2)` IF
        `the practice is prescribed`
    AND `employs someone to carry it out`
    AND (NOT `the employee is qualified`)
    AND NOT (`did not know` AND `exercised due diligence`)

-- s 24(4): "a fine not exceeding $25,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or ... both and, in the case of a
-- second or subsequent conviction, ... $50,000 or ... 12 months".
GIVEN `a second or subsequent conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under section 24` MEANS IF `a second or subsequent conviction` THEN 50000 ELSE 25000

GIVEN `a second or subsequent conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months under section 24` MEANS IF `a second or subsequent conviction` THEN 12 ELSE 6

-- s 25: "A person is not entitled to demand, claim, accept, receive, retain or sue for or recover any fee or charge in any court for
-- any act done in contravention of section 24."
GIVEN `the act contravened section 24` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the fee may be kept or sued for` IF NOT `the act contravened section 24`

§§ `12, 16, 17 -- notifying changes, renewing and surrendering`

-- s 12(3): a registered person must inform the Registrar in writing of any change in name, working address, residential address
-- "within 28 days of the change"; (4) fine up to $1,000. (5): a person who reports a change of residential address under s 10 of
-- the National Registration Act 1965 "is deemed to have complied with subsection (3) relating to residential address on the date on
-- which the person makes the report". (Treating an NRA report within 28 days as timely is an inference from "on the date".)
GIVEN `days until the Registrar was told` IS A NUMBER, `the change is of residential address only` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `days until the change was reported under the National Registration Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the change was notified in time` IF
        `days until the Registrar was told` AT MOST 28
    OR  (`the change is of residential address only` AND `days until the change was reported under the National Registration Act` AT MOST 28)

-- s 17(4): renewal "must be made no later than 30 days before the expiry"; (5) a person who applies "later than 30 days before the
-- expiry ... is liable to pay ... the late application fee". (The fee itself is prescribed by the Board and not in the deposit.)
GIVEN `days before expiry the renewal was made` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a late application fee is payable` IF `days before expiry the renewal was made` LESS THAN 30

-- s 17(7): a practising certificate "is deemed to be cancelled when (a) the registration ... is cancelled or suspended under section
-- 19 or 26A; or (b) an interim order ... is confirmed by the Board under section 26H(8)(a)". (8) surrender "no later than the 14th
-- day after the cancellation"; (9) fine up to $1,000. s 16(2): the certificate of registration is surrendered "within 14 days of
-- being notified" of cancellation or suspension; (3) fine up to $1,000.
DECLARE Event IS ONE OF
    `registration cancelled by the Board`
    `registration suspended by the Board`
    `registration voluntarily cancelled or suspended`
    `an interim order made but not yet confirmed`
    `an interim order confirmed`
    `a caution or censure`
    `a penalty ordered`
    `the class of registration altered`

GIVEN `the event` IS AN Event
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the practising certificate is deemed cancelled` IF
    CONSIDER `the event`
    WHEN `registration cancelled by the Board` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `registration suspended by the Board` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `registration voluntarily cancelled or suspended` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an interim order confirmed` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `days taken to surrender` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the certificate was surrendered in time` IF `days taken to surrender` AT MOST 14

§§ `19 -- cancellation, and what the Board may do instead`

-- s 19(1): the Board may cancel registration if satisfied the person (a) obtained it "by a fraudulent or incorrect statement";
-- (b) had the qualification withdrawn; (c) had a foreign registration withdrawn, suspended or cancelled; (d) has ceased to practise;
-- (e) failed to comply with a registration condition; (f) contravened a conduct regulation; (g) was convicted of an offence
-- "involving fraud or dishonesty"; (h) was convicted of an offence "implying a defect in character"; (i) "has been guilty of any
-- professional misconduct or negligence"; (j) failed to comply with an order under (2)(c), (d) or (g); (k) "improper act or
-- conduct"; (l) "is unable to carry out ... safely or effectively by reason of a mental or physical condition".
DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF
    `registration obtained by a fraudulent or incorrect statement`
    `qualification withdrawn`
    `foreign registration withdrawn`
    `ceased to practise`
    `breach of a registration condition`
    `breach of a conduct regulation`
    `conviction involving fraud or dishonesty`
    `conviction implying a defect in character`
    `professional misconduct or negligence`
    `breach of a Board order`
    `improper act or conduct`
    `unfit by a mental or physical condition`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ground is in section 19(1)(e) to (k)` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `breach of a registration condition` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `breach of a conduct regulation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `conviction involving fraud or dishonesty` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `conviction implying a defect in character` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `professional misconduct or negligence` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `breach of a Board order` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `improper act or conduct` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ground is in section 19(1)(l)` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `unfit by a mental or physical condition` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 19(2): on grounds (1)(e) to (k) the Board may "instead of cancelling" (a) caution or censure; (b) issue a letter of advice;
-- (c) order an undertaking; (d) order a penalty; (e) alter the class of registration; (f) modify conditions "for a period not
-- exceeding 3 years"; (g) refer to mediation; (h) "suspend the registration ... for a period not exceeding 3 years".
-- s 19(3): on ground (1)(l) only (a) suspension "not exceeding 12 months"; (b) altering the class; (c) modifying conditions.
-- On grounds (a) to (d) the Act offers cancellation and nothing short of it.
DECLARE Measure IS ONE OF
    `a caution or censure`
    `a letter of advice`
    `an undertaking`
    `a financial penalty`
    `altering the class of registration`
    `modifying the conditions of registration`
    `mediation with the complainant`
    `suspension`

GIVEN `the measure` IS A Measure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the measure is open under section 19(3)` IF
    CONSIDER `the measure`
    WHEN `suspension` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `altering the class of registration` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `modifying the conditions of registration` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground, `the measure` IS A Measure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may take the measure instead of cancelling` IF
        `the ground is in section 19(1)(e) to (k)` `the ground`
    OR  (`the ground is in section 19(1)(l)` `the ground` AND `the measure is open under section 19(3)` `the measure`)

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the longest suspension in months` MEANS
    IF `the ground is in section 19(1)(e) to (k)` `the ground` THEN 36
    ELSE IF `the ground is in section 19(1)(l)` `the ground` THEN 12
         ELSE 0

-- s 19(2)(d): "(i) a penalty not exceeding $10,000; or (ii) a penalty not exceeding $50,000, if the act or omission ... occurred on
-- or after 1 April 2020".
GIVEN `the conduct occurred on or after 1 April 2020` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum penalty under section 19(2)(d)` MEANS IF `the conduct occurred on or after 1 April 2020` THEN 50000 ELSE 10000

§§ `19(6), (7), 21 -- when a decision takes effect, and appeal`

-- s 19(6): a decision "does not take effect until the 31st day after the date of the decision". (7): a decision TO CANCEL under (1)
-- "takes immediate effect when the Board certifies" a serious and imminent risk to the public, or the need to avoid an actual
-- incident. s 21(3): where the person appeals, the decision, "if not certified under section 19(7), takes effect only when" the
-- High Court confirms it, the appeal is dismissed, or the appeal is withdrawn. Day 0 is the date of the decision.
GIVEN `days since the decision` IS A NUMBER, `the decision is a cancellation under section 19(1)` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `certified under section 19(7)` IS A BOOLEAN, `appealed` IS A BOOLEAN, `the decision was confirmed or the appeal dismissed or withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision has taken effect` IF
        (`the decision is a cancellation under section 19(1)` AND `certified under section 19(7)`)
    OR  (`appealed` AND `the decision was confirmed or the appeal dismissed or withdrawn`)
    OR  ((NOT `appealed`) AND `days since the decision` AT LEAST 31)

-- s 21(1): appeal to the General Division of the High Court "within 30 days of the date of the decision or within any further
-- period that the General Division of the High Court allows"; (2) "There is no appeal from a decision of the General Division".
-- s 15(3): a refusal to register may be appealed "within 30 days of the notice ... to the Minister whose decision is final".
GIVEN `days since the decision` IS A NUMBER, `the High Court allowed a further period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appeal under section 21 is in time` IF
    `days since the decision` AT MOST 30 OR `the High Court allowed a further period`

GIVEN `days since the notice of refusal` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appeal to the Minister against refusal is in time` IF `days since the notice of refusal` AT MOST 30

§§ `23 -- restoration`

-- s 23(3): "No application for re-registration may be made ... (a) before the expiry of 3 years from the date of the cancellation;
-- and (b) more than once in any period of 12 months."
GIVEN `months since the cancellation` IS A NUMBER, `applied in the last 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an application for re-registration may be made` IF
    `months since the cancellation` AT LEAST 36 AND NOT `applied in the last 12 months`

§§ `26A -- voluntary cancellation or suspension`

-- s 26A(1): a registered person may ask the Board in writing if he or she believes (a) fitness to practise is impaired by a mental
-- or physical condition or (b) the quality of services falls below the reasonable standard. (2): the Board may, "with the agreement
-- of the registered person", cancel, suspend (up to 3 years), alter the class or modify conditions. (3): "the Board must not take
-- any action ... if (a) the Board believes that there is evidence of any matter in section 19(1)(g), (h), (i) or (k); or (b) any
-- inquiry under Division 2 has started and is pending".
GIVEN `the person agrees` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Board believes there is evidence of a 19(1)(g), (h), (i) or (k) matter` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `an inquiry is pending` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may act on a voluntary request` IF
        `the person agrees`
    AND (NOT `the Board believes there is evidence of a 19(1)(g), (h), (i) or (k) matter`)
    AND (NOT `an inquiry is pending`)

§§ `26B, 26C -- complaints`

-- s 26B(1): "A person (whether or not a member or an employee of the Board) may make a complaint". (2): it must be in writing and,
-- if it relates to a matter in s 19(1)(e), (f), (i), (k) or (l), "be supported by a statutory declaration unless" made by a public
-- officer or a member or employee of the Board in that capacity.
GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground, `made by a public officer or Board member or employee in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a statutory declaration is required` IF
        (NOT `made by a public officer or Board member or employee in that capacity`)
    AND CONSIDER `the ground`
        WHEN `breach of a registration condition` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `breach of a conduct regulation` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `professional misconduct or negligence` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `improper act or conduct` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `unfit by a mental or physical condition` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 26C(3): the Board may dismiss a complaint "where the Board is unanimously of the opinion that the complaint ... is frivolous,
-- vexatious, misconceived or lacking in substance"; (4) otherwise "the Board must refer the complaint ... to an Inquiry Committee".
GIVEN `the Board thinks it frivolous, vexatious, misconceived or lacking in substance` IS A BOOLEAN, `unanimously` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the complaint must go to an Inquiry Committee` IF
    NOT (`the Board thinks it frivolous, vexatious, misconceived or lacking in substance` AND `unanimously`)

§§ `29(8), 30(5), (6) -- answering an investigator`

-- s 30(5): a person who "without reasonable excuse, fails to do anything required" under s 29(2)(k) or (3)(a) commits an offence
-- ($5,000 or 6 months). (6): "it is a reasonable excuse ... if doing so might tend to incriminate that person". s 29(8): a person
-- "is not subject to a requirement" if he or she (a) does not possess the document or information or (b) has taken all reasonable
-- steps to obtain it and been unable to.
GIVEN `failed to comply` IS A BOOLEAN, `compliance might incriminate` IS A BOOLEAN, `does not possess it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `took all reasonable steps to obtain it` IS A BOOLEAN, `has another reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing an investigator's requirement is an offence` IF
        `failed to comply`
    AND (NOT `compliance might incriminate`)
    AND (NOT `does not possess it`)
    AND (NOT `took all reasonable steps to obtain it`)
    AND (NOT `has another reasonable excuse`)

§§ `34A -- composition`

-- s 34A(1): the Board may compound a prescribed compoundable offence by collecting "a sum not exceeding the lower of ... (a) one
-- half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence; (b) $2,000". Which offences are compoundable is
-- prescribed by regulations not in the deposit.
GIVEN `the maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the largest composition sum` MEANS `the lower of` (`the maximum fine` DIVIDED BY 2) 2000
